Router4's two uplinks (eth4 to router5, eth5 to router3) are administratively down while both peer sides remain fully `UP,LOWER_UP`. This is the classic `link_down` fingerprint: carrier present, frames arriving, drops at ingress because the interface is admin-disabled.

=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: router4
diagnosis_text:
**Affected component:** router4's two uplink interfaces — eth4 (`link_r4_r5`, 192.168.15.2/24, peering with router5) and eth5 (`link_r4_r3`, 172.25.1.1/24, peering with router3) — have been administratively brought down (`link_down` fault).

**Mechanism:** The lab uses RIP as its inter-zone routing protocol. With both uplinks flagged `<BROADCAST,MULTICAST>` and `state DOWN` (no `UP` or `LOWER_UP` bits set), router4's `ripd` daemon cannot send or receive RIP updates on either path to the rest of the routing mesh. As a result, router4's kernel routing table contains only one entry: the directly connected `192.168.200.0/24` (Location C) on eth0. Every packet from a Location C host destined for any other subnet — including Location A's 172.16.10.0/24 and 172.16.20.0/24 — arrives at the gateway (192.168.200.1) and is dropped with ICMP `Destination Net Unreachable`, exactly as observed in the live probe.

**Localization:** router4, interfaces eth4 and eth5. Physical carrier is confirmed present on both (non-zero RX bytes and 15 ingress drops each), while the peer endpoints (router5 eth5 and router3 eth5) remain fully `UP,LOWER_UP`. Router5 is actively transmitting RIP updates toward router4 (4760 bytes TX on eth5), but they are dropped at router4's admin-disabled interface.

**Root cause:** Both uplink interfaces on router4 were administratively shut down, severing router4 from the RIP mesh and making Location C unreachable from — and unable to reach — any other subnet in the topology.

**Fix:** On router4, run `ip link set eth4 up` and `ip link set eth5 up`. RIP adjacencies with router5 and router3 will re-establish within the RIP update interval, and routes to all zones (including Location A) will repopulate in router4's forwarding table.
=== END ===